.PP
See our internal \fRstyle definitions\fP for some more examples\&.
.SS "Changing the default class name"
If you need to use a class name other than \fRprose\fP for any reason, you can do so using the \fRclassName\fP option when registering the plugin:

.PP
.PP
.nf
@import 'tailwindcss';
@plugin "@tailwindcss/typography" {
  classname: wysiwyg;
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Now every instance of \fRprose\fP in the default class names will be replaced by your custom class name:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<article class="wysiwyg wysiwyg\-slate lg:wysiwyg\-xl">
  <h1>My Heading</h1>
  <p>\&.\&.\&.</p>

  <div class="not\-wysiwyg">
    <!\-\- Some example or demo that needs to be prose\-free \-\->
  </div>

  <p>\&.\&.\&.</p>
  <!\-\- \&.\&.\&. \-\->
</article>
.fi
.PP
.SS "Customizing the CSS"
If you want to customize the raw CSS generated by this plugin, you can use the JavaScript based theme API\&. To do that, use the \fR@config\fP directive:

.PP
.PP
.nf
  @import "tailwindcss";
  @plugin "@tailwindcss/typography";
+ @config "\&./tailwind\&.config\&.js";
.fi
.PP

.PP
You can then create your own config by adding a new \fRtailwind\&.config\&.js\fP file with the \fRtypography\fP section and providing your styles under the \fRcss\fP key:

.PP
.PP
.nf
 {{ filename: 'tailwind\&.config\&.js' }}
/** @type {import('tailwindcss')\&.Config} */
module\&.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      typography: {
        DEFAULT: {
          css: {
            color: '#333',
            a: {
              color: '#3182ce',
              '&:hover': {
                color: '#2c5282',
              },
            },
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Like with all theme customizations in Tailwind, you can use CSS variables if you need access to access your theme configuration:

.PP
.PP
.nf
 {{ filename: 'tailwind\&.config\&.js' }}
/** @type {import('tailwindcss')\&.Config} */
module\&.exports = {
  theme: {
    extend: {
      typography: {
        DEFAULT: {
          css: {
            color: 'var(\-\-color\-gray\-800)',
            // \&.\&.\&.
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
Customizations should be applied to a specific modifier like \fRDEFAULT\fP or \fRxl\fP, and must be added under the \fRcss\fP property\&. Customizations are authored in the same \fRCSS-in-JS syntax\fP used to write Tailwind v3 plugins\&.

.PP
See \fRthe default styles\fP for this plugin for more in-depth examples of configuring each modifier\&.

